Vx_GVT = 60 ; km/h
#ENDMYellow

#RingCtrl8 1
NUM_CACHED_RUNS 1
#RingCtrl9 

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#AEB: Autonomous Emergency Braking
#ACC: Automatic Cruise Control
#GVT: Global Vehicle Target
#VUT: Vehicle Under Test (ego vehicle)
#FCW: Forward Collision Warning
#LKAS: Lane-Keeping Assistance System
#CCRm: Car-to-Car Rear, Moving GVT
#
#This ACC example is based on a test scenario published by Euro NCAP for AEB systems with modified conditions. A target is moving at 60 km/h and a variety of speeds are simulated for the vehicle with ACC:
#- No steering controller is used, as LKAS is keeping the vehicle within it's lane, per the Euro NCAP spec.
#- The GVT speed is defined with an output parameter Vx_GVT that can be set as a constant or managed with an equation.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

